  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Mostar Rock School</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Support to Mostar Rock School</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Mostar Rock School (MoRS) bildades 2012 och registrerades som en lokal NGO 2014. Skolan har tre anst&#xe4;llda samt flera musikl&#xe4;rare och tekniker anst&#xe4;llda p&#xe5; deltid. Deras huvudsakliga verksamhet &#xe4;r att ansluta ungdomar i det uppdelade samh&#xe4;llet som Mostar best&#xe5;r av genom musikutbildning och genom en plattform som ger st&#xf6;d till unga musiker och band i Mostar och i en vidare region. MoRS &#xe4;r fortfarande relativt ny i organisationsutveckling och stor del av deras verksamhet &#xe4;r finansierat av givare. Norska ambassaden har gett st&#xf6;d sedan starten med 500 000 NOK. Den andra fasen kommer att separat st&#xf6;djas av Sverige och USAID. &#xc4;ven andra givare &#xe4;r intresserade (Schweiz, Norge).</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The stated goal of the project is to (re)building ties and inter ethnic confidence among Mostar communities.  The MoRS is best described as a social change maker.  The target group is youth who have grown up in a divided post conflict environment.  
The project is relevant from 2 aspects of the Swedish strategy: prevention of discrimination, and reconciliation/conflict reduction.  This is precisely defined under result 13 of the current strategy, promoting trust and reconciliation. 

MoRS is requesting support for core activities of the school for a period of 34 months, starting March 2017. The budget is reasonable and risks are appraised to be acceptable.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project impact goal is defined as &quot;rebuilt ties and improved confidence between Mostar communities, a decrease of tensions and no more negative stereotyping in Mostar region and throughout BiH.  The outcome level goal is to serve as a platform with the range of services for young people promoting MoRS as an example of functional interethnic collaboration</narrative>
  </description>
